ncz-screensavers (0.8.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Three-feature merge onto integration: the Black Hole randomize work, the
    in-house neongravity scene and the per-screensaver gear dialog fix are
    folded into one release branch off 0.8.9 (f7e692c). The ship set and the
    Mali tier/calibration logic are unchanged; no source file from the
    Mali-G720 tier branch was edited.
  * Black Hole: a new `randomize` option re-rolls the look at each screensaver
    start, with a safe envelope per GPU class (off | look | everything).
    everything also re-rolls the scene type and palette inside the catalogue
    and the user's own constraints. The engine pin set honours env/CLI >
    pinned stored > rolled > default, and the launcher marks
    `blackhole-color-mode` pinned whenever it is not the literal vendor
    default `stylized`, so the shipped Cygnus default stays pinned.
    ncz-screensaver-gsettings override ships with
    `hack-options={'blackhole_gles3': {'randomize': 'everything'}}`
    whenever the installed engine lists `randomize` in
    `blackhole_gles3 --dump-schema`; older engines keep the previous
    override. Engine bit: src/blackhole_randomize.{c,h},
    src/gles3_blackhole.c (weak ncz_hack_preinit hook), src/gles3_harness.c
    (hook call site), src/blackhole_opts.h (option row, basic).
    Launcher bit: launcher/ncz-screensaver (BASIC_OPTIONS, NCZ_HACK_PINNED).
    Plugin bit: plugin/screensaver/{screensaver,ncz_backend,backend}.vala
    (Randomize switch, Roll now button, pin lines with Unpin,
    option_is_stored). New test: tests/test_blackhole_randomize.c (30000
    seeded envelope rolls, 20000 pin-respecting rolls, class gating).
    Schema bit: config/dev.ncz.screensaver.gschema.xml (randomize key,
    enum off|look|everything). Docs: docs/BLACKHOLE-RANDOMIZE.md.
  * xshadertoy neongravity: the in-house analytic neongravity scene
    replaces the third-party CC0 neongravity-1 port in ncz_ship_bins;
    ship count unchanged at 74. The in-house shader was already in tree
    but never compiled; it now ships, with xst_common.glsl installed
    alongside it (the first shipped saver that #includes xst_common.glsl;
    install rule tied to the ship set). PROVENANCE.tsv records
    xshadertoy_neongravity as shipped, xshadertoy_neongravity-1,
    universeball and gravitywell as displaced-by:xshadertoy_neongravity.
    New test: tools/tests/test_neongravity_inhouse.py. Docs:
    docs/audit/neongravity-inhouse-2026-10-05.md.
  * Plugin gear: clicking the per-screensaver gear used to append the
    HackOptionsPanel below the entire chooser (up to 74 rows) so it
    landed off the bottom of the page. The panel now opens in a transient
    dialog (Gtk.Window / Gtk.HeaderBar; Close button; modal,
    transient-for the root) so it works regardless of the shell's
    scroller. The inline options_box / configured_id fields are removed;
    the top "Options" button opens the same dialog. The Developer-mode
    empty-state hint ("No basic options; enable Developer options in
    Advanced to see them.") is shown only when the panel has no basic
    row and Developer mode is off, and follows the Developer switch
    while the dialog is open. Headless gear test
    (plugin/screensaver/tests/gear_options_test.vala + tools/test-plugin-gear.sh)
    instantiates the real ScreensaverSettings against the real NczScreensaverBackend
    and checks every catalog hack that ships options in engine 0.8.9.
    Plugin package version is 0.3.16.

