ncz-screensavers (0.8.9+gtk4ref1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference: the reference GTK4 front end now matches
    the engine it drives. It reads the mode, GPU-pool and colour-mode choices
    out of the installed dev.ncz.screensaver schema instead of keeping its own
    copies of those lists, so a new engine key reaches the UI without a code
    change here; the catalogue rows carry the minimum-GPU-class badge the
    engine reports in `ncz-screensaver list --json`; and the per-screensaver
    options dialog gained a "Randomize all" button that fills every option
    inside the range its shipped options/*.tsv declares.
  * ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference: libadwaita is no longer required. GTK4 is
    the only hard dependency (gir1.2-adw-1 moves from Depends to Suggests) and
    every libadwaita widget has a plain GTK4 fallback, so the app starts and
    edits the same schema keys on desktops that ship GTK4 without libadwaita.
    The reference package is still Architecture: all and still not pulled in by
    the engine package, so image hooks that refuse it keep refusing it.
  * ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference: Preview in the options dialog now goes
    through $NCZ_SCREENSAVER_CLI like every other engine call; it used a
    hard-coded launcher name and was a silent no-op on a system where the
    launcher is installed under another name or path. The dead GSK_RENDERER
    default is gone (it warned on GTK >= 4.10, where "ngl" became "gl").
  * ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference: build-time tests. --gtk-smoke builds the
    window and the options dialog on a throw-away display (Xvfb or Broadway)
    and asserts the catalogue loaded and the dialog round-trips; the test suite
    covers the GPU tiers, the schema-derived choice lists, randomize and the
    no-libadwaita path. Both are wired into `meson test --suite
    gtk4-reference-app` and skip (exit 77) where PyGObject, GTK 4 or a display
    is missing.
  * Docs: rewrote contrib/gtk4-reference-app/README.md for a reader outside
    the NCZ-OS image - what the reference front end is, how to build and run it
    on Debian, Fedora and Arch, and how it relates to the engine.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 22:30:00 -0400

ncz-screensavers (0.8.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Licence: the project is now Apache-2.0, ending the GPL-2.0-or-later vs
    Apache-2.0 conflict recorded by the 0.8.7 audit. LICENSE is the pure
    Apache License 2.0 text, a root NOTICE carries the Apache attribution
    convention, meson.build's license field is Apache-2.0, README and the
    package description state the project licence, and debian/copyright is
    rewritten as machine-readable DEP-5 with per-component stanzas. Each
    screensaver remains a separate program, so the vendored and ported
    components keep their own licences. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    headers were added to the NCZ-authored harness, launcher, plugin, tools,
    tests and in-house engines; no third-party header was altered.
  * xshadertoy: the two shipped shaders that declared CC0 but embedded
    snippets of unstated provenance no longer do. neontriangulator's two
    "License: Unknown" hash helpers are replaced with Inigo Quilez's MIT hash
    routines, and the "License: Unknown" Matt Taylor tonemapper in
    neontriangulator and neongravity-1 is replaced with an in-house filmic
    tone curve. The CC0/MIT grants of the shaders themselves are unchanged;
    both stay in the ship set (74 binaries), and no hack was added or removed.
  * xshadertoy neongravity: the in-house analytic neongravity scene now ships,
    replacing the third-party CC0 neongravity-1 port in ncz_ship_bins (ship
    count unchanged at 74). The scene is home-grown NCZ (Apache-2.0, no
    third-party snippet inside) and is validated headless on build-host (amd64,
    Mesa GLES3) and ULTRA (arm64 container); see
    docs/audit/neongravity-inhouse-2026-10-05.md. This makes the 0.8.2
    supersession claim true: xshadertoy_universeball and gravitywell are
    recorded as displaced-by:xshadertoy_neongravity, and the third-party
    neongravity-1 port is displaced-by:xshadertoy_neongravity and builds as a
    developer-only target.
  * Docs: the 0.8.9 correction of the 0.8.2 "displaced by the in-house
    neongravity" claim (which named the third-party port that shipped at the
    time) is superseded by the entry above; PROVENANCE.tsv and
    SHADER-LEDGER.md now record the in-house scene as the shipped one.

