ncz-screensavers (0.8.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * xshadertoy: tier the alienbeacon raymarch by GPU class. Alienbeacon is a
    200-step raymarch whose distance field sums four spiral-noise octave
    series per step; it ran at about 2.5 fps on the Mali-G720 at the 1080 cap
    and under 6 fps at its render hint. The existing NCZ_QUALITY hook (0 weak,
    1 mid, 2 strong) now lowers the march count, noise octaves, shadow steps
    and ambient-occlusion probes on mid and weak GPUs. The strong path is the
    original shader, byte-for-byte. On the reference hardware it goes to
    39.3 fps / p95 28.8 ms on the Mali-G720 and 39.3 fps / 29.4 ms on the
    UHD 630 at scale 0.5; the Navi14 is unchanged at 60 fps.
  * tiers.tsv: re-measured the four legacy classics (crackberg, cubestorm,
    geodesic, datatowers) and xshadertoy_alienbeacon on the reference hosts.
    All five now hold 30 fps with p95 <= 40 ms on the UHD 630 (native and at
    scale 0.5) and on the Mali-G720 at the platform default, so all five move
    from strong to weak. The four classics were already fixed by the 0.8.x
    shader-engine ports (60 fps on both the UHD 630 and the Mali-G720); only
    alienbeacon needed the raymarch tier. RTX 2060 left unmeasured.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400

