ncz-screensavers (0.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * GLES3 harness: pin a linear (non-sRGB) window surface
    (EGL_GL_COLORSPACE_LINEAR) and keep GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB off, so the
    shader's own gamma is the only sRGB encode and the on-screen image
    matches the frame dump. Harness-wide: every GLES3 saver benefits.
  * xshadertoy neonhorizon: rewrite as the period-canonical synthwave look
    (scrolling perspective grid, parallax lit-window skyline, striped sun
    disc, dark sky), with vendor-independent sin-free hashing.
  * xshadertoy: force opaque output (alpha 1.0) in the shared wrapper tail.
    Nine savers (bestill0-0..5-0, darktransit, noxfire, rigrekt) left .a at
    0, so a layer-shell surface composited them to nothing and they looked
    blank even though their RGB was correct.
  * xshadertoy noxfire: the tunnel radius oscillated through zero and the
    unbounded march overflowed d, collapsing the frame to NaN/black on
    some drivers and at different times per vendor. Bound the march,
    reduce the noise angle modulo TAU, keep the tunnel open, and retune the
    exposure to the warm fire palette (mean luma now >= 0.08 at 4 s / 30 s).
  * Black hole: the Cygnus palette (NCZ-OS 26.10 magenta/cyan on
    violet-black) is confirmed present on the integration line
    (--palette=cygnus, NCZ_BLACKHOLE_PALETTE=cygnus, GSettings
    blackhole-color-mode nick "cygnus"); the cix-installer hook 62 default
    keeps working.
  * tests: pin the linear-surface contract, the opaque wrapper tail, and a
    blank-saver render gate (alpha 1.0 / mean luma > 0.05 at 2/12/25 s);
    re-derive the reference-app catalog floor from the real catalogue.

 -- Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0400

